Feature: The report of a command

  With --format json, compile, verify and diff write one object: ok, the problems, and what the
  command found. A key that does not apply is absent. A command with an error does not pass, and
  verify does not pass when a gate fails. urn-forge checks each report against this contract before
  it writes it.

  Scenario: A report of compile gives each generated file
    When I check a "compile_report" with:
      | ok   | files                                                                                              | problems |
      | true | [{"domain": "urn:demo:booking", "status": "wrote", "path": "src/generated/domain.generated.ts"}] | []       |
    Then the value is accepted

  Scenario: A report of verify gives each gate and each problem with its place
    When I check a "verify_report" with:
      | ok   | gates                                                                              | domains                                                                                                    | warnings | problems |
      | true | [{"domain": "urn:demo:booking", "gate": 3, "name": "gherkin", "pass": true, "summary": "3 feature(s)"}] | [{"urn": "urn:demo:booking", "gates": [{"gate": 3, "name": "gherkin", "pass": true, "summary": "3 feature(s)"}]}] | 1        | [{"code": "deprecated-use", "severity": "warning", "file": "domain.manifest.yaml", "line": 12, "path": ["definitions", "note", 0], "domain": "urn:demo:booking", "message": "note uses the deprecated definition text", "fix": "Move the use."}] |
    Then the value is accepted

  Scenario: A report of diff gives each change and the verdict of the versions
    When I check a "diff_report" with:
      | ok   | from  | to    | breaking | changes                                                                                     | allowed | why                     | problems |
      | true | 1.0.0 | 2.0.0 | 1        | [{"class": "breaking", "place": "urn:demo:booking:definition:note", "message": "the definition is removed"}] | true    | the major version is new | []       |
    Then the value is accepted

  Scenario Outline: A report that breaks a rule is not a report
    When I check a "<report>" with:
      | ok   | files   | gates   | domains   | warnings   | breaking   | changes   | problems   |
      | <ok> | <files> | <gates> | <domains> | <warnings> | <breaking> | <changes> | <problems> |
    Then the value is rejected by "<rule>" of "<definition>"

    Examples:
      | rule                | definition     | report         | ok    | files                                                     | gates                                                            | domains                                | warnings | breaking | changes                                         | problems                                                                                          |
      | required            | compile_report | compile_report | true  |                                                           |                                                                  |                                        |          |          |                                                 |                                                                                                   |
